<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2012/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>Comentality.Icons</id>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <title>Icons</title>
    <authors>Comentality</authors>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/comentality/xrm-icons</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/comentality/xrm-icons.git" branch="main" />
    <icon>icon.png</icon>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <description>Search a bundled library of Fluent, Phosphor, Lucide and Tabler icons and set one as a Dataverse table icon, web resource and publish included.</description>
    <releaseNotes>v1.0.0
- Search 18,637 icons from four families with no API key, no account, and no outbound host but Dataverse itself. Fluent, Phosphor, Lucide and Tabler are bundled inside the DLL, all MIT or ISC.
- Search in Dynamics words and get the icon rather than the word: account finds the buildings, contact the people, appointment the calendars, case the headsets.
- The table you pick types the search for you, and says nothing when it cannot say anything true - Payment Term is not a terminal and Social Profile is not a car in profile.
- Narrow the table list to the ones with no icon yet, without another round trip.
- The web resource name follows your environment's own convention rather than this tool's.
- See the icon on light and on dark before you commit, at the size a site map really renders it.
- See it in context draws your icon into a real app's navigation, read from that app's own site map, at sizes measured against a live model-driven app.
- Colour follows the app theme by default, which is what Microsoft asks for in a table icon; a fixed colour is one radio button away.
- One button stores the SVG web resource, points the table's IconVectorName at it, and publishes both in a single call.
- Ctrl+Z takes the write back: the table, the drawing that was written over, and a publish. It never deletes.
- An ATTRIBUTION.html beside the icons credits every one this tool has put there, rebuilt from the icons themselves on every apply.
- The three classic PNG icons too, if you want them. Off by default.
- It says what is wrong before the round trip rather than after it: an icon that paints its own colours, a table locked against customisation, a name Dataverse would refuse.
Full changelog, with screenshots: https://github.com/comentality/xrm-icons/releases/tag/v1.0.0
</releaseNotes>
    <tags>XrmToolBox Dynamics365 CRM PowerPlatform Dataverse Icon Icons SVG WebResource Customization</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework=".NETFramework4.8">
        <dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.7.71" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="bin\Release\net48\Comentality.Icons.dll" target="Plugins\Comentality.Icons.dll" />
    <file src="icon.png" target="icon.png" />
    <file src="..\README.md" target="docs\README.md" />
  </files>
</package>
